{"mathcounts-potw-2026-04-13-01":[{"title":"Substitute","body":"$9 \\,@\\, 4 = 9^2 + \\frac{2 \\cdot 9}{4} = 81 + \\frac{18}{4} = \\frac{324}{4} + \\frac{18}{4} = \\frac{342}{4} = \\frac{171}{2}$.\n\n**Answer: $\\frac{171}{2}$**"},{"title":"Decimals","body":"$81 + 4.5 = 85.5 = \\frac{171}{2}$.\n\n**Answer: $\\frac{171}{2}$**"}],"mathcounts-potw-2026-04-13-02":[{"title":"Substitute","body":"$5 \\# 4 = \\frac{25 - 16 + 20}{8} = \\frac{29}{8}$.\n\n**Answer: $\\frac{29}{8}$**"},{"title":"Split the fraction","body":"$\\frac{A^2 - B^2 + AB}{2B} = \\frac{(A-B)(A+B)}{2B} + \\frac{A}{2} = \\frac{1 \\cdot 9}{8} + \\frac52 = \\frac98 + \\frac{20}{8} = \\frac{29}{8}$.\n\n**Answer: $\\frac{29}{8}$**"}],"mathcounts-potw-2026-04-13-03":[{"title":"Inside first","body":"$4 \\,@\\, 2 = 16 + \\frac{8}{2} = 20$. Then $20 \\# 10 = \\frac{400 - 100 + 200}{20} = \\frac{500}{20} = 25$.\n\n**Answer: 25**"},{"title":"Simplify the outer rule","body":"$A \\# B = \\frac{A^2 - B^2}{2B} + \\frac{A}{2}$. With $A = 20$, $B = 10$: $\\frac{300}{20} + 10 = 15 + 10 = 25$.\n\n**Answer: 25**"}]}